{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40270578",
      "title": "Why Keys Matter When Managing State!",
      "sourceHash": "045b99d84b4d987c03a5b1a50c6e79e8fc42c85e2edbc1952daa096e1ca015d6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.37,
          "en": "Okay, that's now enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "about component functions and how the DOM is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "But it is of course important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "to understand all these things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "But now I wanna take a closer look at state again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 14.4,
          "en": "And one important thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.4,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "which I also already mentioned before in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "But which is super important to understand is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 26.18,
          "en": "that state you register in a component function is scoped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.607,
          "end": 29.43,
          "en": "to that component you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.43,
          "end": 34.43,
          "en": "And also is recreated whenever you reuse this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 38.22,
          "en": "So for example in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.22,
          "end": 41.58,
          "en": "if I create a second counter based on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.58,
          "end": 44.22,
          "en": "that same counter component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.22,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "And I give it an initial count of zero, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "If I do that, then both counters, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 56.97,
          "en": "are based on this code here but every counter receives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.97,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "its own independent counter state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 63.96,
          "en": "This state is not shared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.96,
          "end": 66.84,
          "en": "And therefore if I save that here and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.84,
          "end": 70.95,
          "en": "if I change this first counter, this has no impact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.95,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "on the second counter's value and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 78.78,
          "en": "And this is, of course, a super important concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.78,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "because that's what makes components reusable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "State is scoped to a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 88.44,
          "en": "And if you use the same component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.44,
          "end": 92.75999999999999,
          "en": "to create multiple component instances based on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.75999999999999,
          "end": 97.75999999999999,
          "en": "that function every instance has its own isolated state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.1,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "This is really important to understand and keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 105.24000000000001,
          "en": "However, that's not the entire truth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.24000000000001,
          "end": 110.24000000000001,
          "en": "Instead, state is also tracked by position by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 112.65,
          "en": "And to show you what that means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 117.12,
          "en": "I changed the counter component slightly and attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "you'll find the updated version of that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 126.11,
          "en": "And I changed it to now no longer track the current counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.33,
          "end": 131.33,
          "en": "with its state, but to instead track a list of changes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 132.39,
          "end": 135.09,
          "en": "So my state in this component is now an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 135.09,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "of counter changes where every change is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "simply either plus one or minus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "And then the counter value is calculated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 147.993,
          "en": "by in the end adding up all those changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.01,
          "end": 153,
          "en": "Now as a result, the counter still behaves as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 156.36,
          "en": "But now we can bring in another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.36,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "which I also prepared for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "which is already part of the starting project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 164.043,
          "en": "And that's the counter history component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 168.803,
          "en": "This is simply a component which aims to output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 168.803,
          "end": 173.34,
          "en": "these different button presses, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.34,
          "end": 175.82999999999998,
          "en": "So a list of all the different changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 175.82999999999998,
          "end": 177.75,
          "en": "we made to the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.75,
          "end": 181.8,
          "en": "It does that with help of this history item component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.8,
          "end": 184.2,
          "en": "which is defined in that same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.2,
          "end": 186.93,
          "en": "as the counter history component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.93,
          "end": 189.72,
          "en": "Since this component function only gets used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.72,
          "end": 193.635,
          "en": "by this function here and strictly belongs to this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.635,
          "end": 197.1,
          "en": "And we can now use this counter history component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 197.1,
          "end": 200.696,
          "en": "in this counter component here below this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.696,
          "end": 203.917,
          "en": "by simply adding counter history here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 203.917,
          "end": 207.633,
          "en": "And, of course, also adding this import at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.56,
          "end": 211.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then to counter history,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 211.07999999999998,
          "end": 215.22,
          "en": "you must pass a history prop and you should set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.22,
          "end": 218.64,
          "en": "that equal to the counter changes state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.64,
          "end": 220.323,
          "en": "So, this array of changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 224.01,
          "en": "And if you do that and you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.01,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "you'll notice that if you reload that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "as I increment this counter this list here is output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "And now I can decrement it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 235.07999999999998,
          "en": "And you see those different changes being output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.07999999999998,
          "end": 238.65,
          "en": "here in that list as I make more and more changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.65,
          "end": 242.79,
          "en": "And that allows you to find out why the counter has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.79,
          "end": 246.27,
          "en": "this current value, because you see its history",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.27,
          "end": 250.687,
          "en": "or the history of changes to be precise down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.687,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "Now why did I add that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "Well, because in this counter history component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 262.43,
          "en": "in the history item component, I'm also managing some state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 262.68,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "Some states that simply controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 267.76800000000003,
          "en": "whether a specific item is selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 267.76800000000003,
          "end": 271.71,
          "en": "highlighted, you could say, or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.71,
          "end": 274.44,
          "en": "So I can, for example, click on an item here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 275.79,
          "en": "and it's then highlighted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 275.79,
          "end": 277.53,
          "en": "And we can do this for multiple items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 277.53,
          "end": 279.48,
          "en": "and also turn this off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 279.48,
          "end": 281.52,
          "en": "But you'll notice something interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.52,
          "end": 283.92,
          "en": "if I click on this item here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.92,
          "end": 288.09000000000003,
          "en": "And I then click increment or decrement again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 288.09000000000003,
          "end": 291.9,
          "en": "If I do that, you now see that it's still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.9,
          "end": 294.87,
          "en": "the second item that's highlighted here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.87,
          "end": 296.7,
          "en": "But, of course, that's the wrong item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.7,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "now because it should be this item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 300.18,
          "en": "that should be highlighted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.18,
          "end": 303.873,
          "en": "Because that was the item I selected before, a second ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.28,
          "end": 306.72,
          "en": "I can show this to you again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.72,
          "end": 310.98,
          "en": "If I unselect this and select this and click a button, boom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.98,
          "end": 312.42,
          "en": "It's now again the wrong item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.42,
          "end": 316.59,
          "en": "the plus one instead of the minus one that's being selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.59,
          "end": 320.73,
          "en": "And how can this be the case if state belongs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.73,
          "end": 323.25,
          "en": "to a concrete component instance?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.25,
          "end": 327.573,
          "en": "How can it then jump across component instances?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 328.47,
          "end": 332.76,
          "en": "Well, because as mentioned, it's also tracked by position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.76,
          "end": 337.26,
          "en": "So yes, the component instance or to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 337.26,
          "end": 339.45,
          "en": "the type of the component matters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 343.05,
          "en": "So in this case that it's a history item, but then it's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 343.05,
          "end": 347.52,
          "en": "the position of that component instance that also matters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 347.52,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "And the state does not just belong to this component type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 354.903,
          "en": "but also to the position where this component is used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 356.58,
          "end": 359.13,
          "en": "Now for the counters, this was no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 359.13,
          "end": 361.11,
          "en": "I had two counters here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 361.11,
          "end": 364.44,
          "en": "and they never ever changed their position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 364.44,
          "end": 366.75,
          "en": "So therefore the state belongs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.75,
          "end": 370.26,
          "en": "to the type counter and to the positions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 370.26,
          "end": 373.5,
          "en": "And since they never changed, everything is fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 373.5,
          "end": 376.62,
          "en": "But for the counter history, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 376.62,
          "end": 379.95,
          "en": "Since new items are inserted here at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 379.95,
          "end": 381.93,
          "en": "all the other items move down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 381.93,
          "end": 384.42,
          "en": "with every new item that's added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 384.42,
          "end": 385.89,
          "en": "And therefore the position",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 385.89,
          "end": 389.52,
          "en": "of the history item component instances changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 389.52,
          "end": 393.3,
          "en": "And therefore since React behaves the way it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 393.3,
          "end": 396.06,
          "en": "and state belongs to the position",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 396.06,
          "end": 400.71,
          "en": "as well as the component type, the state here jumps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 400.71,
          "end": 403.35,
          "en": "from this component to this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 403.35,
          "end": 405.78,
          "en": "if I click increment again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 405.78,
          "end": 409.47,
          "en": "You see previously it was this component that was selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 409.47,
          "end": 410.913,
          "en": "Now it's this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 411.89,
          "end": 415.35,
          "en": "And that, of course, can be a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 415.35,
          "end": 417.72,
          "en": "because in most cases you don't want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 417.72,
          "end": 419.90999999999997,
          "en": "the state to jump like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 419.90999999999997,
          "end": 422.49,
          "en": "And therefore React also gives you a mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 422.49,
          "end": 426.993,
          "en": "that allows you to avoid this, this key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 426.993,
          "end": 431.04,
          "en": "Because this is a problem that typically only occurs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 431.04,
          "end": 434.73,
          "en": "in lists like this because it can only occur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 434.73,
          "end": 439.35,
          "en": "if you have sibling components that are of the same type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 439.35,
          "end": 443.79,
          "en": "and the number or position of those components may change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 443.79,
          "end": 446.28,
          "en": "And that's for example, not the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 446.28,
          "end": 447.78,
          "en": "But it is the case here",
